# libretranslate
msgid "**Agents as employees, with a kernel between them and the host.** *web-app-hermes* and *web-app-openclaw* deploy agents behind the single sign-on gate, wired to the gateway's models and to the MCP servers discovery hands them, each proving on deploy that it can actually reach them. *svc-virt-kata* runs that tier under a kernel-isolating container runtime, and *svc-ai-robot* embodies an agent on a dedicated device. Every sandboxed agent acts as its own platform account rather than borrowing yours. See [web-app-hermes](roles/web-app-hermes/README.md), [web-app-openclaw](roles/web-app-openclaw/README.md) and [svc-virt-kata](roles/svc-virt-kata/README.md)."
msgstr "**Axentes como empregados, cun núcleo entre eles e o anfitrión.** *Web-app-hermes* e *Web-app-openclaw* Despregue axentes detrás da porta de sinalización única, conectado aos modelos da porta de entrada e ao descubrimento dos servidores MCP mans, cada proba no despregamento que realmente pode chegar a eles. *svc-virt-kata* corre ese tier baixo un contenedor de illamento do kernel, e *svc-ai-robot* Incorpora un axente nun dispositivo dedicado. Cada axente sandboxed actúa como a súa propia conta de plataforma en vez de prestar a súa. Ver [Web-app-hermes](roles/web-app-hermes/README.md), [Web-app-openclaw](roles/web-app-openclaw/README.md) e [svc-virt-kata](roles/svc-virt-kata/README.md)."

# libretranslate
msgid "**Agents consume tools as MCP clients via the [025](025-mcp-role-integration.md) mechanism.** Hermes and OpenClaw are configured as MCP clients of the repository's MCP server roles over HTTP/SSE (not stdio: under microVM isolation and multi-node placement a stdio subprocess cannot reach an MCP server in another container). Discovery and credentials reuse 025's [`roles_with_service`](../../plugins/lookup/roles_with_service.py) lookup and `credentials:` blocks. Both roles are added to 025's MCP audit as client roles. Only 025's shared contract (the `services.mcp` schema) and the lookup extension are prerequisites for this requirement; 025's audit tooling, full lint set, and baserow+openwebui slice are independent later work."
msgstr "**Os axentes consumen ferramentas como clientes de MCP [025](025-mcp-role-integration.md) mecanismo.** Hermes e OpenClaw están configurados como clientes MCP dos roles do servidor MCP do repositorio sobre HTTP/SSE. (Non stdio: baixo illamento microVM e colocación multi-nodo un subproceso stdio non pode chegar a un servidor MCP noutro recipiente.)Descubrimento e reutilización de credenciais 025's [`roles_with_service`](../../plugins/lookup/roles_with_service.py) Miradas e `credentials:` bloques. Ambos roles son engadidos a 025A auditoría MCP como funcións de cliente. Sólo 025Contrato compartido (El `services.mcp` Esquema) e a extensión de busca son requisitos previos para este requisito; 025A ferramenta de auditoría, o conxunto de revestimento completo e o corte baserow+openwebui son independentes despois do traballo."

# libretranslate
msgid "**Agents that spin up containers use nested Docker inside the isolated runtime; host socket passthrough is forbidden.** When an agent needs to run compose workloads (see the scenario below), it runs a nested Docker daemon inside its own isolated runtime. Mounting the host `/var/run/docker.sock` into an agent that executes model-generated code is **forbidden**: it grants root-equivalent host control and defeats the isolation entirely. Nested Docker costs performance and, on gVisor, may need `runsc` with the appropriate platform; the role README MUST document the overhead. An agent role that requires containers MUST declare this capability explicitly."
msgstr "**Os axentes que xiran contenedores usan Docker aniñado dentro do tempo de execución illado; o pase de toma de hóspedes está prohibido.** Cando un axente debe executar cargas de traballo (Ver o escenario de abaixo), corre unha daemon de Docker no seu propio tempo de execución illado. Montando o hóspede `/var/run/docker.sock` un axente que executa o código xerado polo modelo é **prohibido**Proporciona un control equivalente a raíces e derrota o illamento por completo. Nested Docker custa o rendemento e, en gVisor, pode ser necesario `runsc` coa plataforma adecuada; o papel README debe documentar a cabeza superior. Unha función de axente que require contedores debe declarar esta capacidade explicitamente."

