# libretranslate
msgid "OpenClaw's own CLI reference says so directly: `openclaw mcp serve` \"starts a stdio MCP server\" whose process \"the MCP client owns\". Every HTTP transport in that document belongs to the opposite direction, `openclaw mcp add --url --transport streamable-http`, which is OpenClaw acting as a client. Hermes is the same shape: both entry points, `mcp_serve.py` and `agent/transports/hermes_tools_mcp_server.py`, run the MCP SDK's stdio transport, the repository defines neither `run_streamable_http_async` nor `sse_app`, and the user-facing MCP guide describes only Hermes consuming external servers."
msgstr "A referencia CLI de OpenClaw di así: `openclaw mcp serve` \"Inicia un servidor stdio MCP\" cuxo proceso \"Cliente MCP\"Todo o transporte HTTP nese documento pertence á dirección oposta. `openclaw mcp add --url --transport streamable-http`, É dicir, OpenClaw actúa como cliente. Hermes ten a mesma forma: os dous puntos de entrada `mcp_serve.py` e `agent/transports/hermes_tools_mcp_server.py`, executar o transporte de stdio do MCP SDK, o repositorio non define `run_streamable_http_async` nin tampouco `sse_app`, A guía MCP orientada ao usuario describe só a Hermes consumindo servidores externos."

